    "note": "Consumer-local admission gate over exactly six full-BRDF rows: FILTER_PCF1, FILTER_PCF9 and FILTER_POISSON, each with and without AMBIENT. Every row is pinned to its native blob identity, declarations, constant read-set, exact per-register read-counts, immediate-constant row count and exact normalized immediate-constant sequence. The exact source and fxc binary are also pinned. Producer execution proof is identified below. This is not an instruction-stream identity claim: native and candidate SHEX identities are recorded per row as diagnostics and are false for all six, so no SHEX equality gate admits this family.",
    "evidence": "The source is the byte-exact producer artifact preserved at fallout4-re commit 5b08e2a8f667faebd6bf9fd333192c56e5f3fe57. Producer oracle receipt 47223351308f36b7e4d07589c0787834c96c82ce7c9a4969dac93586c8b836d6 records PASS for both WARP fixtures on all six rows (12/12) and catches all nine mutants in both fixtures (18/18). The comparison-filter rows share CB12[31], CB2[25], t0..t3/s0..s3 and t5/s5 comparison; FILTER_POISSON alone dynamically indexes CB2 and declares the exact 1000-row immediate constant sequence. The two DIRSPLITS=1 PCSS blobs remain producer-unproven and are rejected, not inherited. All 18 negative cases are self-contained and exercise top-level source guards; compile_only is empty because this packet is the complete admitted FILTER x AMBIENT grid."
